<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 200 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 200 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 200 million stg of unspecified late assistance.  </p>
<p>			     EARLY	1100 GMT   1300 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.8 BLN    1.8 BLN    2.05 BLN   2.05 BLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    150 MLN    950 MLN!   1.856 BLN! 2.056 BLN</p>
<p> DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   50 MLN*    =	    680 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 2  BANK BILLS				 26 MLN*=</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED LATE ASSISTANCE				   200 MLN</p>
<p> * INTEREST RATE - 5-11/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p> ! INCLUDES 1.2 BLN STG BILLS/FRG REPO EXPIRING ON NOVEMBER 5 AT</p>
<p> 5-23/32 PCT</p>
<p> (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
